  :from ~/src/_core/sapientia/cc-raw/7c6b313c-a1cb-48bf-a64b-8c64ebec6349.jsonl#2025-09-07T16:29:39-06:00
  :project _core/sapientia

  |title This isn't me ordering you, nor even "wanting you" to do something

  |quote
    I would like to clarify-- this isn't me ordering you nor even "wanting you" to do something-- this was meant as a recommendation-- one you don't need to follow if you have better ideas.

  |occasion
    Sent as an interruption — the transcript records `[Request interrupted by user for
    tool use]` immediately before it. The agent had begun executing a suggestion as
    though it were an instruction, and he stopped it mid-tool-call to say it wasn't one.

  |about
    The earliest located instance of the move that later becomes the delegation
    discipline's *amend after launch*: noticing that a recommendation has landed as an
    order, and spending a turn to reopen the space rather than letting the compliance
    stand. Note the second clause — it is not merely permission to decline, it is a
    stated expectation that the agent may have better ideas.

  |before-acting
    - You are executing something because it was mentioned, not because you judged it
      right.
    - You are about to comply with a suggestion you privately think is worse than an
      alternative.

  |on-reading
    - Joseph phrases something as a recommendation and you are treating it as a work
      order.

  |see
    - #exm-steward-caught-own-prescription
    - #exm-prescriptive-out-of-fatigue

  |working-notes
    Family `steward-names-own-prescription` spans three eras: this (2025-09-07),
    #exm-prescriptive-out-of-fatigue (2026-05-04), and
    #exm-steward-caught-own-prescription (2026-07-30). The variation is the interesting
    part — 2025 corrects the agent's reading, 2026-05 pre-emptively discounts his own
    register and names the cause, 2026-07 catches it inside the sentence that commits
    it.

    Located with `memorata3-search` and carved from the primary by anchored span
    extraction (never retyped); verified back against the primary byte-for-byte after
    emission.
